{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q007_chey_like_function_divergence","answer":"In the current public SCOPe base release 2.08 (latest periodic label 2.08-2026-08-16), these are three distinct families within the CheY-like superfamily c.23.1 (SUNID 52172): CheY-related c.23.1.1 (SUNID 52173), ornithine-decarboxylase N-terminal “wing” c.23.1.4 (SUNID 52252), and the KaiA N-terminal domain c.23.1.5 (SUNID 82344). All also lie in the broader flavodoxin-like fold c.23 and alpha/beta class c. The API explicitly marks homology as implied at the superfamily level, so SCOPe supports remote common ancestry and a conserved structural core—not same-family membership, close orthology, or interchangeable function.

Function must not be transferred across these families. The ODC wing and KaiA N-terminal domain cannot be called canonical CheY-type receiver domains merely from this relationship: it does not establish phospho-Asp chemistry, histidine-kinase recognition, a two-component phosphorelay, or response-regulator output. Conversely, CheY-related proteins and the ODC wing cannot be assigned KaiA-specific circadian/KaiC regulation. Nor does the relationship confer ornithine-decarboxylase activity, PLP chemistry, substrate binding, or catalytic residues on CheY-related or KaiA domains—or even show that the isolated ODC wing is independently catalytic. SCOPe assigns the ODC major domain separately to c.67.1.5 (SUNID 53444), confirming that the shared CheY-like lineage concerns the auxiliary N-terminal wing rather than the main catalytic domain.

A cross-family member may therefore serve as a remote template for the overall CheY-like fold, but not for active-site, phosphotransfer, ligand-binding, interaction, or whole-protein functional annotation. Functional modeling should prefer a same-family representative with matching domain boundaries and biological context and require independent sequence-conservation and biochemical/genetic evidence.","evidence_used":["pretrained model knowledge","/api/v1/","/api/v1/openapi.yaml","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CheY&mode=prefix&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=ornithine%20decarboxylase&mode=token&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=KaiA&mode=prefix&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=KaiA%20N-terminal&mode=token&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=circadian&mode=prefix&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52252","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52252/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52172/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52173","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/82344","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52172/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52173/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52252/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/82344/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53444"]}]}
